Subject: Cantor Schema Direction Data Design

@ [design_uuid] 46a88126-ab19-42f9-8525-02222ca0f191

& [SchemaContractDirection] is closed
  + input_deserialize
  + output_serialize

& [ContractDefinitionAccount] is inspectable
  + direction
  + stable_type_name
  + semantic_type_id
  + local_definition_pointer
  + direct_local_reference_targets
  + raw_content_digest
  + contract_fingerprint
  + semantic_residual_ids

& [Bundle] contains two isolated maps
  + input_definitions keyed by stable type name and generated with Deserialize
  + output_definitions keyed by stable type name and generated with Serialize
  + document-local $defs and fragment references retain ordinary stable type names
  + bundle lookup uses direction before type name, avoiding direction syntax inside JSON Pointer tokens

& [FingerprintPreimage] is domain separated
  + UTF-8 profile id cantor-schema-contract-definition/0.1
  + zero byte separator
  + canonical direction token
  + zero byte separator
  + stable type name
  + zero byte separator
  + normalized definition bytes

& [RootAssignments] are exact
  + prepare_input, run_input, and verify_input use input_deserialize
  + base_response and preparation_response use output_serialize
  + future roots must declare direction before generation

